# S1: STALL/TTFT arm A of AB (A = c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix; B = c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-traffic, Lever N + prefix reuse on the traffic profile). stall8_cold128k and stall8_cold262k (seven decoders and ONE cold arrival) and cold2_254k (six decoders and TWO simultaneous
# 254k arrivals: eight seats). READ per pair (G-NP5): the arrival's TTFT, every seat's longest gap, the decoders' tok/s inside the arrival window, the f_eff lines (the deadline governor binding), hashes equal across the arms
# (levern_compare.py). PASS: the worst seat gap at most 10 s (the control stalled about 100 s), every decoding seat progressed inside the window, arrival TTFT at most 200 s; KILL: any TTFT over 240 s or any seat gap at least the
# control's; cold2_254k: both TTFTs at most 240 s and the second at most the control's second plus 15 s (the gaps are reported). ARC runners at zero. Measured basis: stall8_cold262k 7.3 minutes (v532).
# TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the W-2 window pack (tp4-w2-levern-jobs: Lever N robustness, then the cutover; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/stage1-windows and push the job's tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Names no rig, card, host or registry. ORDER.txt has the order,
# the classes, the minutes, the boxes, the tags and every rule. C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-11 is the window image (the combined branch's engine with the Lever N traffic profile baked in as its
# default); a job that names tp4-serve-10 runs the production base image. C2_BOX_MINUTES is the job's box: the workflow enforces it from inside, it never cancels a run.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-11
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,stall8_cold128k,stall8_cold262k,cold2_254k
C2_BOX_MINUTES=50
